|  We use the term family court to refer to any trial-level court handling domestic relations matters, such as divorce, custody, visitation, or child support. In
|  some states these courts are called by the name Family Court. In many jurisdictions, specific matters of child abuse and neglect are heard exclusively by the
|  Juvenile Courts or Children’s Courts. In some states these matters are heard by
.  trial courts of general jurisdiction.2


