|  The mother told Amy Neustein that she had feared losing custody of her
|  sons, despite the serious allegations of abuse, because of the extraordinary
|  camaraderie between the law guardian and the children’s father, who appeared pro se throughout a two-week trial. The law guardian not only zealously
|  cross-examined the mother’s witnesses but called - as her own witness - a CPS
|  caseworker to testify that the mother had neglected her children by making
|  false charges of sexual abuse. That camaraderie did not pay off for the father
.  in this particular case.9


