p: .
t. 
|  A typical regulation in New Jersey specifies that one of the purposes of CPS
|  is to [p]reserve and strengthen family life: New Jersey Administrative Code
|  10:133C-2.3(a)(2); N.J.S.A. 30:4C-1(a). This principle means that family ties
|  must be encouraged and preserved to the greatest extent possible under the
.  circumstances of a given case.4


