p: .
t. 
|  In the case of a Brooklyn, New York, mother, the judge instructed CPS to charge
|  the mother with neglect because she had changed therapists for her sexually
|  abused children without first seeking the permission of the court. Even if her
|  actions were in violation of a court order (for which contempt remedies could
|  have been sought), her actions certainly did not qualify as neglect under the
.  statute. See Pagnozzi, Mom Was Trying to Help Her Kids.28


