|  The only other population where there is a rush to place children in foster care
|  is the Orthodox Jewish population. There, prejudices arise because for a mother
|  to bring a charge of sexual abuse against an Orthodox man poses a threat to the
|  tightly organized patriarchal structure of that society. By stripping the child of
|  its mother, the thorny issue of sex abuse is swept under the rug, which is sine
